# Line endings.
#
# Everything is LF in the repository. The exception is PowerShell: it is
# Windows-native and some versions are unhappy with LF-only scripts, so .ps1
# files are checked out with CRLF and stored that way. Without this pin, a
# Windows checkout and a macOS checkout disagree about every .ps1 and every
# commit looks like it rewrote them.
#
# The matching symptom on the other side: a shell script that fails with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" has been given CRLF line endings.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never mangle these.
*.hex binary
*.uf2 binary
*.bin binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
